{"name":"Brushed Metal","hex":"#c7c8c9","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brushed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Roughened by rubbing with an abrasive brushes, especially as a finish.","Having been cleaned, tidied, or straightened with a brush."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of brush"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brushed"},{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.","A light tincture used in a coat of arms, specifically argent (white or silver) and or (gold)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Brushed metal","blocks":[{"text":"Brushed stainless steel or dull polished metal is metal with a unidirectional satin finish. It is produced by polishing the metal with a 120–180 grit belt or wheel then softening with an 80–120 grit greaseless compound or a medium non-woven abrasive belt or pad."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Brushed_Aluminium.jpg/330px-Brushed_Aluminium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brushed_metal","wikidata":"Q4979723"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal","wikidata":"Q11426"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Brushed_Aluminium.jpg/500px-Brushed_Aluminium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Brushed_Aluminium.jpg/1280px-Brushed_Aluminium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Brushed_Aluminium.jpg/500px-Brushed_Aluminium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A piece of brushed aluminium","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrushed_Aluminium.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Breville.jpg/500px-Breville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Breville.jpg/1280px-Breville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Breville.jpg/500px-Breville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A collection of brushed stainless steel Breville small appliances","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABreville.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delorean_dmc12_front.jpg/500px-Delorean_dmc12_front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delorean_dmc12_front.jpg/1280px-Delorean_dmc12_front.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delorean_dmc12_front.jpg/500px-Delo